          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As represented, the MCU supply pins have no power connection, so the processors cannot operate. The separate +3.3V and +3V3 nets also mean the regulator output does not supply the +3V3 loads.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The UART3 connector's TX net is connected to FCC1 pin 48 (VCAP), and its RX net to FCC1 pin 73 (VCAP). Both MCU pins are VCAP, not UART pins.",
      "expected": "UART3 connector signals should connect to MCU UART TX/RX GPIO pins. VCAP pins should have the required core-regulator decoupling capacitors, not serve as interface signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "UART3 is not connected to usable UART pins, and external activity on the connector is applied to the MCU's core-regulator output pins, risking malfunction or damage.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0-Pad5)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1-Pad6)", "VREF+_FCC"],
      "observed": "FCC crystal nets connect to FCC1 pins 5 (PE6) and 37 (PE7), rather than its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC crystal nets have no connection to NAVC1; its PH0 and PH1 pins instead connect to separate capacitor nets, and FCC1 pin 13 (PH1) is also on VREF+_FCC.",
      "expected": "The specified 25 MHz HSE crystals should connect to each MCU's HSE oscillator pins (PH0/PH1), with those pins dedicated to the oscillator circuit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"VREF+_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"PH1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has the intended external crystal connection; the NAVC crystal is disconnected from its oscillator pins, and FCC oscillator pins are misrouted. The MCUs may fall back to internal clocks or fail to start as intended, and FCC's PH1 oscillator pin is repurposed onto the reference net.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs' supply pins are unconnected, FCC UART3 is routed to VCAP pins, and the HSE crystal connections do not reach the intended oscillator pins. These connectivity faults contradict the specified powered dual-MCU design and its crystal requirements."
}

